   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_04">Kreuzstrasse 19</name> <hi rend="superscript">III</hi>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zürich</name> VIII</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>(<name type="geo" key="G_CHE">Switzerland</name>)</addrLine> </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear Miss <name type="person" key="weav76">Weaver</name>: Many thanks for your kind card of <date when="1916-02-19">19 instant</date>. I am very glad to hear that you have now found a printer who will <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">print <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">my text</rs>
                        </seg> as I wrote it and I hope that I shall soon see it in print. <name type="person" key="poun85">Mr Pound</name> writes me that he hopes <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">your firm</seg> will become an English <name type="work">
                            <hi rend="underline">Mercure</hi> <hi rend="underline">de</hi> <hi rend="underline">France</hi>
                        </name>. I hope so too and wish you every success.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1916-02-25">25/ii/916</date>
                        </dateline> </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The firm of Richard Clay &amp; Sons had agreed to print <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name> for Harriet Shaw Weaver. Within a few weeks, they backed out.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Following the end of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">The Egoist</name>’s serial publication of <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>, Weaver had intended to publish the complete book at her own expense under the imprint of The Egoist Ltd, but was thwarted by the reluctance of English printers who feared prosecution for the publication of a text that was considered obscene.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
